### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### VALIDACIONES Y CASOS DE ERROR
###
### Pre-requisito: existe un admin (admin@docklite.local) y al menos
### un user con role USER. Ejecuta primero los Logins para tokens.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@host = http://localhost:8080
@apiV1 = {{host}}/api/v1


### Login admin → token en {{tokenAdmin}}
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@docklite.local",
  "password": "admin1234"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenAdmin", response.body.token);
%}


### Login user → token en {{tokenUser}}
### Ajusta el email/password al de un user real (ej. uno creado vía invitation)
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rafa@test.com",
  "password": "rafa1234"
}

> {%
client.global.set("tokenUser", response.body.token);
%}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### AUTH — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 401 — Login con password incorrecta
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@docklite.local",
  "password": "passwordmal"
}


### 401 — Login con email que no existe (mismo mensaje, no filtramos info)
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noexiste@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 404 — POST /auth/register ya no existe (modelo invitation-only)
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "x",
  "email": "x@x.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### INVITATIONS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 404 — Validar token inexistente
GET {{apiV1}}/invitations/no-existe-este-token


### 404 — Aceptar token inexistente
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/no-existe/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "x",
  "email": "x@x.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 403 — USER intenta crear invitación
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}


### 401 — Crear invitación sin token
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}


### Pre-paso: admin crea invitación, después la cancela y luego se intenta usar
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}

> {%
client.global.set("cancelTestToken", response.body.token);
client.global.set("cancelTestId", response.body.id);
%}


### Cancelar la invitación recién creada
DELETE {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations/{{cancelTestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}


### 404 — Validar invitación cancelada
GET {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{cancelTestToken}}


### 404 — Aceptar invitación cancelada
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{cancelTestToken}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "tarde",
  "email": "tarde@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### Pre-paso: agotar invitación
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}

> {%
client.global.set("usedToken", response.body.token);
%}


### Acepta una vez (consume el único uso) — guarda email distinto cada vez
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{usedToken}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "victima1",
  "email": "victima1@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 404 — Aceptar otra vez (ya está agotada)
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{usedToken}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "victima2",
  "email": "victima2@test.com",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 409 — Aceptar con email duplicado
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}

> {%
client.global.set("dupToken", response.body.token);
%}


### 409 — Mismo email ya existe
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{dupToken}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "otroAdmin",
  "email": "admin@docklite.local",
  "password": "123456"
}


### 400 — Validaciones (username corto, email mal, password corta)
POST {{apiV1}}/admin/invitations
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxUses": 1
}

> {%
client.global.set("validationToken", response.body.token);
%}


### Validation failed con campos detallados
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{validationToken}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "x",
  "email": "no-es-email",
  "password": "12"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### USERS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 401 — sin token
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me


### 401 — token inválido
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer chorizo-no-valido


### 401 — header sin "Bearer "
GET {{apiV1}}/users/me
Authorization: {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — USER intenta listar todos los users
GET {{apiV1}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 401 — PUT /me con password actual incorrecta
PUT {{apiV1}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "passwordmal",
  "newPassword": "nuevapass1"
}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### CONTAINERS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 400 — Crear sin imagen (falla validación @NotBlank)
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "sin-imagen",
  "autoStart": true
}


### 400 — Crear con body totalmente vacío
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


### 401 — Listar sin token
GET {{apiV1}}/containers


### 404 — Inspect container inexistente
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/no-existe-este-id
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}


### Pre-paso para 403 cross-user: admin crea container
POST {{apiV1}}/containers
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "image": "nginx:alpine",
  "name": "admin-protegido",
  "autoStart": true
}

> {%
client.global.set("adminContainerId", response.body.id);
%}


### 403 — userb intenta inspeccionar container de admin
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta parar container de admin
POST {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta borrar container de admin
DELETE {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### 403 — userb intenta ver logs de container de admin
GET {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### Limpieza: admin borra el container que creó arriba
DELETE {{apiV1}}/containers/{{adminContainerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### IMAGES — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 403 — USER intenta borrar imagen (solo admin)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/images/nginx:alpine
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenUser}}


### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### NETWORKS — errores
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### 400 — Borrar red default (bridge)
### Primero hay que sacar el id de bridge
GET {{apiV1}}/networks
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}


### 400 — Borrar bridge (sustituye <BRIDGE_ID> por el id real)
# DELETE {{apiV1}}/networks/<BRIDGE_ID>
# Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}
